<title>UK: Ex-dividends take 2.344 points off UK FTSE index.</title>
<headline>Ex-dividends take 2.344 points off UK FTSE index.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The London Stock Exchange said the following FTSE-100 stocks trade ex-dividend from Monday and this will depress the FTSE by 2.344 points.</p>
<p>					     DIVIDEND	INDEX</p>
<p>						(PENCE)	EFFECT</p>
<p> COMPANY				   Net   Gross   Gross</p>
<p> * BAA				     4.50   5.625   0.341</p>
<p> * Boots				   6.20   7.750   0.410</p>
<p> * British Airways		     4.25   5.313   0.311</p>
<p> * British Steel			 3.00   3.750   0.447</p>
<p> * Unilever			     10.29  12.863   0.613</p>
<p> * Whitbread			     6.25   7.813   0.222</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 5106</p>
</text>
